yosys: abc_new tells a given -script from "-script" in a path

abc_new collects every option that takes a value, values included,
into one string and decided whether -script was given by searching that
string for "-script". A liberty path under a directory such as
OpenROAD-flow-scripts, a -constr path or a -dont_use name containing
"-script" therefore switched off abc_new's default script: abc9_exe
fell back to abc9.script.default, a LUT script (&if -v; &mfs), and
mapping to cells failed ("ABC returned unmapped node") or produced no
mapping ("Missing mapping (no 'M' section)").

The argument loop now records that it parsed -script.

Reported as YosysHQ/yosys#6320, with a reproducer; YosysHQ asks for
issues, not LLM-written fixes, so this patch is carried here only.
test/yosys_abc_new_script_path reproduces it. bazel-orfs's own paths
never contain "-script", so no flow here changes; ORFS's layout does,
which is what ORFS #4664's CI tripped over. Retires at the bump onto a
BCR yosys that fixes #6320.

--- a/passes/techmap/abc_new.cc
+++ b/passes/techmap/abc_new.cc
@@ -100,11 +100,14 @@
 		std::string run_from, run_to;
 		cleanup = true;
 		size_t argidx;
+		bool script_given = false;
 		for (argidx = 1; argidx < args.size(); argidx++) {
 			if (args[argidx] == "-exe" || args[argidx] == "-script" ||
 					args[argidx] == "-D" ||
 					args[argidx] == "-constr" || args[argidx] == "-dont_use" ||
 					args[argidx] == "-liberty" || args[argidx] == "-genlib") {
+				if (args[argidx] == "-script")
+					script_given = true;
 				abc_exe_options += " " + args[argidx] + " " + args[argidx + 1];
 				argidx++;
 			} else if (args[argidx] == "-run" && argidx + 1 < args.size()) {
@@ -122,7 +125,7 @@
 		extra_args(args, argidx, d);
 
 		// If no script provided, use a default.
-		if (abc_exe_options.find("-script") == std::string::npos) {
+		if (!script_given) {
 			d->scratchpad_set_string("abc9.script", RTLIL::constpad["abc_new.script.speed"]);
 		}
 
